---
{
  "layout": "main",
  "title": "About Us",
  "description": "Learn about Grokipedia Wiki's mission, transparent methodology, and independent team dedicated to objective encyclopedia analysis.",
  "keywords": "about grokipedia wiki, our mission, analysis methodology, independent review team",
  "path": "/about/",
  "breadcrumbs": [
    {"label": "About Us"}
  ]
}
---

{{> breadcrumb}}

<section class="section pt-24">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="text-center mb-16">
        <h1 class="heading-1 mb-6">About Grokipedia Wiki</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground">
          Independent, objective, and transparent encyclopedia comparison
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Mission -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="heading-2 mb-6">Our Mission</h2>
        <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Grokipedia Wiki is an independent third-party analysis platform dedicated to providing comprehensive,
            objective comparisons between Grokipedia and Wikipedia. We believe that transparency and rigorous
            analysis are essential for understanding how different encyclopedia platforms handle information,
            especially on controversial or sensitive topics.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Our goal is to help readers make informed decisions about which sources to trust by providing
            detailed, data-driven analysis of editorial practices, source quality, and factual accuracy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Methodology -->
      <div id="methodology" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="heading-2 mb-6">Our Methodology</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="heading-3 mb-3">1. Source Analysis</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We examine all cited sources for credibility, reliability, and relevance. Each source is
              verified and rated according to established journalistic standards.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="heading-3 mb-3">2. Content Comparison</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We compare content side-by-side, identifying differences in framing, emphasis, and factual
              claims. Our analysis highlights areas of agreement and divergence.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="heading-3 mb-3">3. Editorial Practice Review</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              We investigate the editorial processes behind each entry, including contributor backgrounds,
              review mechanisms, and update frequency.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="card p-6">
            <h3 class="heading-3 mb-3">4. Bias Detection</h3>
            <p class="text-muted-foreground">
              Using both manual review and AI-powered tools, we identify potential biases in language,
              source selection, and content presentation.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Independence -->
      <div class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="heading-2 mb-6">Our Independence</h2>
        <div class="card p-8 bg-primary/5 border-primary/20">
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-4">
            Grokipedia Wiki is <strong>not affiliated</strong> with Grokipedia, Wikipedia, or any encyclopedia platform.
            We maintain complete editorial independence and receive no funding from any encyclopedia project.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted-foreground">
            Our analysis is conducted objectively, and our conclusions are based solely on verifiable evidence
            and established analytical frameworks.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Section -->
      <div id="faq" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="heading-2 mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">

          <!-- FAQ 1 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>Is Grokipedia Wiki affiliated with Grokipedia or Wikipedia?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>No, Grokipedia Wiki is completely independent and not affiliated with either Grokipedia or Wikipedia. We are a third-party analysis platform dedicated to providing objective comparisons between the two encyclopedia platforms. We receive no funding from either organization and maintain complete editorial independence.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- FAQ 2 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>How do you ensure objectivity in your analysis?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>Our analysis methodology is fully transparent and documented. We base all conclusions on verifiable evidence from credible news sources (CNN, TIME, PBS, Wired, Fortune, etc.) and direct examination of both platforms. We present findings from multiple perspectives and clearly distinguish between documented facts and analysis. All sources are cited in our articles.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- FAQ 3 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>Why did you create this comparison platform?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>When Grokipedia launched in October 2025 as an AI-powered alternative to Wikipedia, we recognized the need for independent, objective analysis comparing these platforms. With both facing allegations of bias (in opposite directions) and fundamental differences in their approaches, we created this platform to provide the detailed, evidence-based comparisons that users need to make informed decisions about which encyclopedia sources to trust.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- FAQ 4 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>Are your analysis articles peer-reviewed?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>Our articles undergo rigorous internal review to ensure accuracy and fairness. We base our analysis on reporting from established news organizations and direct platform examination. While not formally peer-reviewed in the academic sense, we welcome feedback and corrections from readers through our contact form. We update articles when new information emerges or when readers identify errors.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- FAQ 5 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>How often do you update your analysis?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>We continuously monitor developments with both Grokipedia and Wikipedia. Our current articles include scheduled review dates, and we update content when significant changes occur on either platform or when new evidence emerges. Major updates are announced in our News Center.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          <!-- FAQ 6 -->
          <details class="card p-6 group">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-lg flex items-center justify-between">
              <span>Can I suggest topics for future analysis?</span>
              <svg class="h-5 w-5 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-4 text-muted-foreground">
              <p>Yes! We welcome suggestions for topics you'd like us to analyze. Please use our contact form below to submit ideas. We prioritize topics that are timely, significant, and where comparison would provide valuable insights to our readers.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- FAQ Schema -->
      <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Is Grokipedia Wiki affiliated with Grokipedia or Wikipedia?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "No, Grokipedia Wiki is completely independent and not affiliated with either Grokipedia or Wikipedia. We are a third-party analysis platform dedicated to providing objective comparisons between the two encyclopedia platforms. We receive no funding from either organization and maintain complete editorial independence."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How do you ensure objectivity in your analysis?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Our analysis methodology is fully transparent and documented. We base all conclusions on verifiable evidence from credible news sources (CNN, TIME, PBS, Wired, Fortune, etc.) and direct examination of both platforms. We present findings from multiple perspectives and clearly distinguish between documented facts and analysis. All sources are cited in our articles."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Why did you create this comparison platform?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "When Grokipedia launched in October 2025 as an AI-powered alternative to Wikipedia, we recognized the need for independent, objective analysis comparing these platforms. With both facing allegations of bias (in opposite directions) and fundamental differences in their approaches, we created this platform to provide the detailed, evidence-based comparisons that users need to make informed decisions about which encyclopedia sources to trust."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Are your analysis articles peer-reviewed?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Our articles undergo rigorous internal review to ensure accuracy and fairness. We base our analysis on reporting from established news organizations and direct platform examination. While not formally peer-reviewed in the academic sense, we welcome feedback and corrections from readers through our contact form. We update articles when new information emerges or when readers identify errors."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "How often do you update your analysis?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "We continuously monitor developments with both Grokipedia and Wikipedia. Our current articles include scheduled review dates, and we update content when significant changes occur on either platform or when new evidence emerges. Major updates are announced in our News Center."
            }
          },
          {
            "@type": "Question",
            "name": "Can I suggest topics for future analysis?",
            "acceptedAnswer": {
              "@type": "Answer",
              "text": "Yes! We welcome suggestions for topics you'd like us to analyze. Please use our contact form below to submit ideas. We prioritize topics that are timely, significant, and where comparison would provide valuable insights to our readers."
            }
          }
        ]
      }
      </script>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div id="contact" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="heading-2 mb-6">Contact Us</h2>
        <div class="card p-8">
          <p class="text-muted-foreground mb-6">
            Have questions, suggestions, or want to report an issue with our analysis? We'd love to hear from you.
          </p>

          <form data-form="contact" class="space-y-4">
            <div>
              <label for="name" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2">Name</label>
              <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required class="input w-full" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="email" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2">Email</label>
              <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required class="input w-full" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="message" class="block text-sm font-medium mb-2">Message</label>
              <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5" required class="input w-full resize-none"></textarea>
            </div>

            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-full">
              Send Message
            </button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Disclaimer -->
      <div class="text-center text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <p>
          For our full disclaimer and terms of service, please visit
          <a href="/disclaimer/" class="link">Disclaimer</a> and
          <a href="/terms/" class="link">Terms</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
